762
00:30:55,500 --> 00:30:58,167
- [Mike] You can make a
lot of money wrestling.

763
00:30:59,933 --> 00:31:01,967
- You haven't
understood anything.

764
00:31:01,967 --> 00:31:04,033
- [Tom] Oh I didn't know
there that many landmines

765
00:31:04,033 --> 00:31:05,633
left in Narnia.

766
00:31:05,633 --> 00:31:08,200
(upbeat music)

767
00:31:13,600 --> 00:31:16,400
- Ah but I like it, too.

768
00:31:16,400 --> 00:31:19,867
- Hello, tell me what good
deeds can I do for you?

769
00:31:19,867 --> 00:31:21,367
(screaming)

770
00:31:21,367 --> 00:31:22,133
- [Mike] Well you could stop
crapping on our playground

771
00:31:22,133 --> 00:31:23,533
for one.

772
00:31:23,533 --> 00:31:24,533
- Stop!

773
00:31:24,533 --> 00:31:27,533
Wait.
(screaming)

774
00:31:27,533 --> 00:31:29,067
Don't run away.

775
00:31:29,067 --> 00:31:29,767
- [Tom] He's outrunning a
really slow quarter horse

776
00:31:29,767 --> 00:31:31,033
at this point.

777
00:31:31,033 --> 00:31:34,467
- Wait, I want to do
a good deed for you.

778
00:31:34,467 --> 00:31:35,300
Wait.

779
00:31:36,300 --> 00:31:37,700
Wait!

780
00:31:37,700 --> 00:31:38,967
- When animals attack.

781
00:31:38,967 --> 00:31:40,433
- [Mike] Now it will
go into slow motion

782
00:31:40,433 --> 00:31:42,633
and you'll hear Barbers
Adagio for strings

783
00:31:42,633 --> 00:31:44,033
as he tears them apart.

784
00:31:46,933 --> 00:31:48,833
- [Tom] And he falls
right on bear plop.

785
00:31:50,900 --> 00:31:52,167
- Um, Ricola?

786
00:31:53,300 --> 00:31:54,100
Muxinex?

787
00:31:55,267 --> 00:31:57,600
- [Mike] Charlie was
close, I could feel it.

788
00:31:59,033 --> 00:32:00,467
- [Tom] Oh there's my wallet.

789
00:32:02,367 --> 00:32:06,000
- As the Easter egg hunt
goes into its 48th week.

790
00:32:06,000 --> 00:32:07,967
(growling)

791
00:32:07,967 --> 00:32:10,400
- [Mike] Friend good.

792
00:32:10,400 --> 00:32:12,233
(growling)

793
00:32:12,233 --> 00:32:13,633
- [Tom] Ah the perfect
speaker stand, finally.

794
00:32:13,633 --> 00:32:15,733
- And here's that footstool
I've always wanted.

795
00:32:17,500 --> 00:32:18,833
- [Mike] Aw, you know?

796
00:32:18,833 --> 00:32:21,267
(all cooing)

797
00:32:24,700 --> 00:32:27,867
I'll take this back to the
lab, see if its edible or not.

798
00:32:29,433 --> 00:32:30,833
- [Tom] Hurry, the DNR's coming.

799
00:32:30,833 --> 00:32:32,900
Load up the truck
and get out of here.

800
00:32:32,900 --> 00:32:34,067
(growls)
(screaming)

801
00:32:34,067 --> 00:32:36,533
- Icky boys, ew.

802
00:32:36,533 --> 00:32:38,900
- [Mike] Delayed
reaction syndrome.

803
00:32:38,900 --> 00:32:41,933
(shouting)

804
00:32:41,933 --> 00:32:43,567
- There's a bear there.

805
00:32:43,567 --> 00:32:45,033
- [Tom] Quick, there's
a sale on babushkas

806
00:32:45,033 --> 00:32:46,700
at Bloomingdale-skis.

807
00:32:46,700 --> 00:32:49,467
(laughs)

808
00:32:49,467 --> 00:32:50,833
- Chernobyl's exploding again.

809
00:32:50,833 --> 00:32:52,000
Let's go watch.

810
00:32:53,467 --> 00:32:55,567
- [Tom] I could watch this
scene play out all day.

811
00:32:56,633 --> 00:32:57,400
Well.

812
00:32:58,433 --> 00:33:00,700
- [Mike] How not to be seen.

813
00:33:00,700 --> 00:33:03,200
(soft classical music)

814
00:33:03,200 --> 00:33:06,267
- So what, are we looking
for Waldo here or what?

815
00:33:06,267 --> 00:33:08,200
- [Tom] Antony, Antony!

816
00:33:09,400 --> 00:33:10,633
- [Mike] Its prince
spaghetti today here

817
00:33:10,633 --> 00:33:12,000
in the Italian north
end of the swamp.

818
00:33:13,633 --> 00:33:17,100
- Good morning, little flowers,
little flowers on the stump.

819
00:33:17,100 --> 00:33:18,700
- Yeah, you got the money?

820
00:33:20,800 --> 00:33:23,133
- [Mike] Oh just make
yourself at home.

821
00:33:23,133 --> 00:33:25,033
- Every single day
I come to see you.

822
00:33:25,033 --> 00:33:28,000
Every single day I
come to talk to you.

823
00:33:28,000 --> 00:33:29,600
I hope that I'm
not bothering you.

824
00:33:29,600 --> 00:33:30,867
- [Tom] Have a seat
in the waiting room,

825
00:33:30,867 --> 00:33:32,933
one of our flowers will
be with you in a moment.

826
00:33:33,800 --> 00:33:35,533
- Its all right?
- its okay.

827
00:33:35,533 --> 00:33:38,133
You in, I'm in love with you.

828
00:33:38,133 --> 00:33:39,067
- Tell me, little flowers.

829
00:33:39,067 --> 00:33:40,800
Is Ivan still living today?

830
00:33:40,800 --> 00:33:42,533
- [Tom] Uh definitely, yes.

831
00:33:42,533 --> 00:33:43,367
- I don't know?
- Yeah, uh, I don't know.

832
00:33:43,367 --> 00:33:44,300
Come back tomorrow.

833
00:33:44,300 --> 00:33:45,267
- [Mike] You want to take this?

834
00:33:45,267 --> 00:33:46,667
- He's alive?

835
00:33:46,667 --> 00:33:47,900
- We didn't say that.

836
00:33:47,900 --> 00:33:50,433
- He must be angry
with me, I suppose.

837
00:33:51,867 --> 00:33:53,300
- [Tom] I need to check with
our flowers on the street.

838
00:33:54,900 --> 00:33:57,033
- You mean he's not?

839
00:33:57,033 --> 00:33:58,933
- [Mike] Hey look, I'm just
asking for straight answers.

840
00:33:58,933 --> 00:34:01,233
Don't bust my chops, man.

841
00:34:01,233 --> 00:34:03,300
- Now tell me,
will we ever meet?

842
00:34:03,300 --> 00:34:05,533
- Our lawyers have
advised us not to comment.

843
00:34:07,833 --> 00:34:09,567
- [Tom] Ew, what
am I kneeling in?

844
00:34:11,100 --> 00:34:14,167
- Yes, look for the
answer in the algae.

845
00:34:15,600 --> 00:34:18,667
- [Mike] From the land
of sky blue waters.

846
00:34:19,867 --> 00:34:21,600
(growling)

847
00:34:21,600 --> 00:34:23,100
- [Tom] I mean where
else are you gonna do it

848
00:34:23,100 --> 00:34:24,400
but in the woods?

849
00:34:25,967 --> 00:34:28,000
- Charity, dear little sisters,

850
00:34:28,000 --> 00:34:29,533
dear little brothers, charity.

851
00:34:29,533 --> 00:34:30,167
Dear little sisters, dear
little brothers, charity.

852
00:34:32,633 --> 00:34:34,300
Give us plasms, for without us

853
00:34:34,300 --> 00:34:36,300
you could not
prove your charity.

854
00:34:36,300 --> 00:34:38,667
- Oh great, Shakespeare
in the park.

855
00:34:38,667 --> 00:34:41,600
- Give to a poor orphan
who is homeless, penniless,

856
00:34:41,600 --> 00:34:42,967
crippled, and blind.

857
00:34:42,967 --> 00:34:45,133
Give to the poor, the blind

858
00:34:45,133 --> 00:34:46,300
and the deaf mute.
- How much have you

859
00:34:46,300 --> 00:34:47,533
in your cup?
- Not a copper, not--

860
00:34:47,533 --> 00:34:50,800
- Well if that's the
case, here's a copper.

861
00:34:50,800 --> 00:34:51,867
- [Tom] Now shut up.

862
00:34:51,867 --> 00:34:54,467
- Oh to do a good deed.

863
00:34:54,467 --> 00:34:57,167
I suppose that one
copper isn't enough.

864
00:34:58,467 --> 00:34:59,733
Where are you going?

865
00:34:59,733 --> 00:35:00,700
- A werewolf!

866
00:35:01,600 --> 00:35:03,500
Run for your lives.

867
00:35:03,500 --> 00:35:05,900
- [Mike] Regain your sight
and grow your leg back.

868
00:35:05,900 --> 00:35:07,267
- A werewolf!

869
00:35:07,267 --> 00:35:08,700
- A werebear actually.

870
00:35:08,700 --> 00:35:10,233
- A werewolf!

871
00:35:10,233 --> 00:35:12,900
- [Tom] Like you're such a hunk.

872
00:35:14,900 --> 00:35:18,700
- What kind of a good
deed will I have to do?

873
00:35:18,700 --> 00:35:20,800
- What kind of bear am I?

874
00:35:22,000 --> 00:35:25,067
- [Mike] Yogurt is
not a finger food.

875
00:35:25,067 --> 00:35:26,700
- How sweet?

876
00:35:26,700 --> 00:35:28,367
Naska, lets have the braid.

877
00:35:28,367 --> 00:35:29,400
Quickly.
- Duty consultant,

878
00:35:29,400 --> 00:35:30,400
Mrs. Khrushchev.

879
00:35:30,400 --> 00:35:31,967
- Here.

880
00:35:31,967 --> 00:35:32,900
- Mama.

881
00:35:32,900 --> 00:35:35,033
Why not smear her eyebrows?

882
00:35:35,033 --> 00:35:38,567
- Why is she putting
Bisquick on her face?

883
00:35:38,567 --> 00:35:40,067
(laughing)

884
00:35:40,067 --> 00:35:43,267
- [Mike] Why are you so mean
to me, Tanta Ernest Borgnine?

885
00:35:43,267 --> 00:35:45,900
- Oh how lovely you look.

886
00:35:47,367 --> 00:35:48,867
- Mama.

887
00:35:48,867 --> 00:35:50,367
- [Tom] Don't let your
babies grow up to be cowboys.

888
00:35:50,367 --> 00:35:52,267
- Naska's braid is
nicer than mine.

889
00:35:52,267 --> 00:35:53,433
- Yours is worth more.

890
00:35:53,433 --> 00:35:54,667
It was bought at the fair.

891
00:35:54,667 --> 00:35:56,600
- I want you to cut off
her braid at the root.

892
00:35:56,600 --> 00:35:58,467
- What could I drag
her by without a braid

893
00:35:58,467 --> 00:35:59,433
on her head, I ask?

894
00:35:59,433 --> 00:36:00,733
- Cut it off.
- Wait, I know.

895
00:36:00,733 --> 00:36:02,067
I'll put a rag over
her braid to hide it.

896
00:36:02,067 --> 00:36:05,067
- All right, then, hide it.

897
00:36:05,067 --> 00:36:06,667
- Alfalfa's greatest role.

898
00:36:08,600 --> 00:36:10,467
- [Mike] I should have
these caterpillars removed.

899
00:36:10,467 --> 00:36:13,400
- Ah you (speaks Russian)

900
00:36:13,400 --> 00:36:15,133
its much easier than working.

901
00:36:15,133 --> 00:36:16,200
- Munchen guzzle?

902
00:36:16,200 --> 00:36:17,600
What the hell?

903
00:36:17,600 --> 00:36:18,600
(laughs)

904
00:36:18,600 --> 00:36:19,767
- There you go.

905
00:36:19,767 --> 00:36:21,567
See, now you're
dressed for housework

906
00:36:21,567 --> 00:36:24,100
and now, my darling,
you put this on.

907
00:36:25,300 --> 00:36:26,933
- [Tom] Its a Burger
King birthday crown.

908
00:36:26,933 --> 00:36:30,233
- Like a princess, darling.

909
00:36:30,233 --> 00:36:32,733
Exactly like a princess.

910
00:36:32,733 --> 00:36:34,100
- Really?

911
00:36:34,100 --> 00:36:36,000
- [Mike] I am pretty
hot, aren't I?

912
00:36:38,067 --> 00:36:39,167
- A princess.

913
00:36:40,900 --> 00:36:42,300
- A little red.

914
00:36:42,300 --> 00:36:45,433
- And now a bag over the
head completes the look.

915
00:36:45,433 --> 00:36:46,733
- I'm all tired out.

916
00:36:46,733 --> 00:36:48,367
I'm sweating.
- Learn to suffer.

917
00:36:48,367 --> 00:36:50,867
- [Mike] Like having Andrea
Dworkin make you over.

918
00:36:51,733 --> 00:36:53,167
- No, not a princess.

919
00:36:53,167 --> 00:36:55,233
- [Tom] She's got that
healthy clown glow.

920
00:36:55,233 --> 00:36:56,100
- Oh no?

921
00:36:57,367 --> 00:36:59,733
- You are a queen.

922
00:36:59,733 --> 00:37:01,500
- [Mike] In that you look
like Freddie Mercury.

923
00:37:01,500 --> 00:37:04,200
- She should just start
over from gene one.

924
00:37:08,967 --> 00:37:12,567
- What kind of a
good deed can I do?

925
00:37:12,567 --> 00:37:15,200
- [Tom] Maybe negotiate
lasting peace in the Mideast?

926
00:37:15,200 --> 00:37:19,100
- [Mike] She's on her way back
from her stick distributor.

927
00:37:19,100 --> 00:37:20,200
- [Tom] Not a very good canoe.

928
00:37:20,200 --> 00:37:22,233
- I can't walk another step.

929
00:37:22,233 --> 00:37:25,400
- Poor granny, here
let me help you.

930
00:37:25,400 --> 00:37:29,067
- Yes, my boy, help me and
it will be a good deed.

931
00:37:29,067 --> 00:37:30,067
- It will be a good deed?

932
00:37:30,067 --> 00:37:31,000
- Help me.

933
00:37:31,000 --> 00:37:32,167
- Boy, I'd be glad to help.

934
00:37:32,167 --> 00:37:33,867
I need to do a good deed.

935
00:37:33,867 --> 00:37:35,533
I need to very badly.
- and this is.

936
00:37:35,533 --> 00:37:36,767
- Get on.

937
00:37:36,767 --> 00:37:38,167
- Where do I get on?

938
00:37:38,167 --> 00:37:39,533
- On my back.
- On your back?

939
00:37:39,533 --> 00:37:41,200
- Climb on.

940
00:37:41,200 --> 00:37:42,967
- Its light-bear transit.

941
00:37:42,967 --> 00:37:44,533
- Do you live far
from here, granny?

942
00:37:44,533 --> 00:37:46,700
- Oh yes, very very far.
- And?

943
00:37:46,700 --> 00:37:48,800
- Its up the mountain,
and then down again,

944
00:37:48,800 --> 00:37:50,833
and up the mountain
on the other side.

945
00:37:50,833 --> 00:37:52,867
- That's all very good.

946
00:37:52,867 --> 00:37:54,700
- Well if you think
so, that's fine.

947
00:37:54,700 --> 00:37:55,833
But don't get all in a sweat.

948
00:37:55,833 --> 00:37:57,900
- Here we go.
- Giddy up, let's go.

949
00:37:57,900 --> 00:37:58,733
- [Tom] Babe!

950
00:38:00,067 --> 00:38:01,433
(mock sobbing)

951
00:38:01,433 --> 00:38:03,033
Oh, Babe.

952
00:38:03,033 --> 00:38:05,533
- Knits all the time,
except in the morning

953
00:38:05,533 --> 00:38:08,367
when she gulps down her
tea and lights the fire

954
00:38:08,367 --> 00:38:09,433
and gets the breakfast.

955
00:38:09,433 --> 00:38:10,800
Then she mops the floor,

956
00:38:10,800 --> 00:38:12,567
and then when the
breakfast is ready she--

957
00:38:12,567 --> 00:38:14,000
- I tell you, she's a marvel.

958
00:38:14,000 --> 00:38:15,633
She's perfect in every respect

959
00:38:15,633 --> 00:38:18,633
and no dream princess
could be lovelier.

960
00:38:18,633 --> 00:38:20,967
- [Mike] And she's
available for sale or lease.

961
00:38:22,133 --> 00:38:24,200
- This matchmaker
can certainly talk.

962
00:38:24,200 --> 00:38:26,900
I think there was
something else we wanted.

963
00:38:26,900 --> 00:38:28,167
- Yes.

964
00:38:28,167 --> 00:38:29,667
- We hear you have
another daughter.

965
00:38:29,667 --> 00:38:33,600
- Good lord, people say
the craziest things.

966
00:38:33,600 --> 00:38:35,100
I am mama's only daughter.

967
00:38:35,100 --> 00:38:36,633
The other ones not my sister.

968
00:38:36,633 --> 00:38:38,500
- That's all right, we'll
have a look at the other one,

969
00:38:38,500 --> 00:38:40,300
if you don't mind.

970
00:38:40,300 --> 00:38:41,800
- Mama.

971
00:38:41,800 --> 00:38:44,200
- Uh oh, there's a ripple in
the daughter market today.

972
00:38:44,200 --> 00:38:45,133
- Well all right.

973
00:38:45,133 --> 00:38:48,467
You'll see her since you insist.

974
00:38:48,467 --> 00:38:49,300
Nastenka.

975
00:38:50,333 --> 00:38:51,167
Nastenka.

976
00:38:52,233 --> 00:38:53,500
Nastenka.

977
00:38:53,500 --> 00:38:56,500
- [Tom] Quick, put
the dog in a dress.

978
00:38:56,500 --> 00:38:57,333
- Naska.

979
00:38:58,300 --> 00:38:59,133
Come here.

980
00:39:00,367 --> 00:39:01,300
- [Mike] Well thanks
for listening.

981
00:39:01,300 --> 00:39:03,733
Its just my fleas got me down.

982
00:39:03,733 --> 00:39:06,067
- Get in there you little viper.

983
00:39:06,067 --> 00:39:07,267
- Somebody needs viping.

984
00:39:08,667 --> 00:39:12,833
- Nastenka, sweetheart
of mine, my honey child.

985
00:39:12,833 --> 00:39:16,400
Come, let these
folks look at you.

986
00:39:16,400 --> 00:39:19,433
- [Tom] Larry Drake
and Vanessa Redgrave.

987
00:39:19,433 --> 00:39:24,133
- No, matchmaker, this
one won't do at all.

988
00:39:24,133 --> 00:39:26,800
She looks like a scarecrow.

989
00:39:26,800 --> 00:39:29,600
- [Mike] Now get out there and
do something Russo-Finnish.

990
00:39:29,600 --> 00:39:33,000
- Our little idiot is
really horrible looking.

991
00:39:33,000 --> 00:39:34,800
- Geeze.
- Her father.

992
00:39:34,800 --> 00:39:37,033
- I uh--
(growls)

993
00:39:37,033 --> 00:39:38,133
I won't.

994
00:39:38,133 --> 00:39:38,967
I'll be quiet.

995
00:39:38,967 --> 00:39:40,433
- Cabbage burp.

996
00:39:40,433 --> 00:39:43,500
- All right, now start
the feast my dear guests.

997
00:39:43,500 --> 00:39:45,067
- That's what I've
been waiting for.

998
00:39:45,067 --> 00:39:46,700
I drink to your health.

999
00:39:46,700 --> 00:39:48,967
- That's all very well but
my son likes goose giblets.

1000
00:39:48,967 --> 00:39:49,900
That's his favorite dish.

1001
00:39:49,900 --> 00:39:51,133
- Ah yes.

1002
00:39:51,133 --> 00:39:53,067
- [Mike] Oh Andy
goose giblets, oh.

1003
00:39:53,067 --> 00:39:54,500
- Naska.

1004
00:39:54,500 --> 00:39:55,867
- Oh no, your lovely daughter
should take care of it.

1005
00:39:55,867 --> 00:39:57,433
Its up to her.

1006
00:39:57,433 --> 00:39:58,667
That's the custom, you know?

1007
00:39:58,667 --> 00:39:59,900
- Mama.

1008
00:39:59,900 --> 00:40:01,600
- That way my son and
I can see what kind

1009
00:40:01,600 --> 00:40:03,000
of a bride we're getting.

1010
00:40:03,000 --> 00:40:05,400
- [Tom] Someday
I'll be a real boy.

1011
00:40:05,400 --> 00:40:08,000
(upbeat music)

1012
00:40:11,867 --> 00:40:13,367
- Well, Tom, I suppose we
ought to check in on those two

1013
00:40:13,367 --> 00:40:14,867
and make sure there's no--
- Little problem here, guys.

1014
00:40:14,867 --> 00:40:16,267
I'm a bear.

1015
00:40:16,267 --> 00:40:17,633
- Oh I'm so sure.

1016
00:40:17,633 --> 00:40:19,133
- Yeah, I'm a bear.

1017
00:40:19,133 --> 00:40:22,600
That little uh, you know, that
that mushroom head elf guy,

1018
00:40:22,600 --> 00:40:23,433
you know?
- yeah.

1019
00:40:23,433 --> 00:40:24,267
- He did it.

1020
00:40:24,267 --> 00:40:25,500
- Oh, huh.

1021
00:40:25,500 --> 00:40:28,033
And where did this happen?

1022
00:40:28,033 --> 00:40:30,367
- Just, you know, around.

1023
00:40:30,367 --> 00:40:32,300
Some luck, huh?

1024
00:40:32,300 --> 00:40:35,800
- You sure you just didn't
hot glue some fur to yourself?

1025
00:40:35,800 --> 00:40:37,367
- Hey, I wish.

1026
00:40:38,500 --> 00:40:40,767
- Yeah, well, huh a bear.

1027
00:40:40,767 --> 00:40:42,100
Well we better check
in on these two,

1028
00:40:42,100 --> 00:40:43,933
see how the peace
process is going.

1029
00:40:43,933 --> 00:40:44,800
- Bear (laughs).

1030
00:40:44,800 --> 00:40:46,200
What a feeb.

1031
00:40:46,200 --> 00:40:47,967
(growls)

1032
00:40:47,967 --> 00:40:50,933
(slobbery munching)

1033
00:40:55,233 --> 00:40:56,267
- Sorry.

1034
00:40:59,900 --> 00:41:01,400
- Well.

1035
00:41:01,400 --> 00:41:02,300
Thank you.

1036
00:41:02,300 --> 00:41:03,500
- You're welcome

1037
00:41:03,500 --> 00:41:06,733
and thank you for
laundering your cape.

1038
00:41:06,733 --> 00:41:09,133
- Oh well, think nothing of it.

1039
00:41:11,267 --> 00:41:12,933
- Would you like
some mashed banana?

1040
00:41:12,933 --> 00:41:14,100
- Oh no, no, no.

1041
00:41:14,100 --> 00:41:15,633
- You sure about that?

1042
00:41:15,633 --> 00:41:17,200
Its nice and rotten.

1043
00:41:17,200 --> 00:41:19,833
I don't eat it till the
fruit flies come a buzzing.

1044
00:41:19,833 --> 00:41:21,300
That's good eating.

1045
00:41:21,300 --> 00:41:22,400
- I'm sure that it is.

1046
00:41:23,233 --> 00:41:24,233
Yum.

1047
00:41:24,233 --> 00:41:26,300
(laughs)

1048
00:41:30,433 --> 00:41:32,600
- So, what are you up to?

1049
00:41:32,600 --> 00:41:35,700
- Oh I'm reading the
entire galactic library

1050
00:41:35,700 --> 00:41:38,100
of the Venusian
Eight system at once,

1051
00:41:38,100 --> 00:41:39,300
with my mind.

1052
00:41:39,300 --> 00:41:40,733
- Oh nice.

1053
00:41:40,733 --> 00:41:42,867
Are there pictures?

1054
00:41:42,867 --> 00:41:45,733
- Several trillion, yes.

1055
00:41:45,733 --> 00:41:46,533
- Oh.

1056
00:41:48,633 --> 00:41:50,133
Oh say, uh.

1057
00:41:50,133 --> 00:41:51,467
My toes feeling better.

1058
00:41:51,467 --> 00:41:54,167
Most of the seepage is dried up.

1059
00:41:54,167 --> 00:41:55,867
- Well, hallelujah.

1060
00:42:01,967 --> 00:42:04,500
- Do you...

1061
00:42:04,500 --> 00:42:06,567
Do you find that, uh,

1062
00:42:06,567 --> 00:42:11,200
well that the Lawgiver
can be mean sometimes?

1063
00:42:12,433 --> 00:42:15,233
- Well, its against
my culture to gossip.

1064
00:42:15,233 --> 00:42:17,067
- Oh sure, but do you?

1065
00:42:18,733 --> 00:42:21,700
- Yes, she can really be a
stone cold witch sometimes.

1066
00:42:21,700 --> 00:42:24,733
- Oh I know and she can
be so condescending.

1067
00:42:24,733 --> 00:42:26,633
- Oh preciously, its
like, oh I'm so great

1068
00:42:26,633 --> 00:42:27,567
and I don't have...

1069
00:42:27,567 --> 00:42:29,033
- Oh would you look at that?

1070
00:42:29,033 --> 00:42:30,400
It looks like that two finally
found something in common.

1071
00:42:30,400 --> 00:42:31,467
- Mike, help!

1072
00:42:32,867 --> 00:42:35,100
Crow ate half of me and
then buried me in the dirt.

1073
00:42:35,100 --> 00:42:36,033
- Mm, not bad.

1074
00:42:36,033 --> 00:42:37,467
- Crow, what is wrong with you?

1075
00:42:37,467 --> 00:42:39,067
- Well I told you,
Mike, I'm a bear.

1076
00:42:39,067 --> 00:42:41,500
- No, no haven't we talked
about this a hundred times

1077
00:42:41,500 --> 00:42:44,500
about you taking your bear
simulations to the extreme?

1078
00:42:44,500 --> 00:42:45,433
- Uh yeah.

1079
00:42:45,433 --> 00:42:47,000
- And what are you doing?

1080
00:42:47,000 --> 00:42:49,633
- Uh taking my bear
simulation to the extreme?

1081
00:42:49,633 --> 00:42:51,100
- There, now do you
see a connection?

1082
00:42:51,100 --> 00:42:52,567
- No.

1083
00:42:52,567 --> 00:42:53,533
- Oh.

1084
00:42:53,533 --> 00:42:54,900
Okay, well let me explain.

1085
00:42:54,900 --> 00:42:55,733
See, when you're a bear you
(alarm buzzing)

1086
00:42:55,733 --> 00:42:56,933
oh we got movie sign.

1087
00:42:56,933 --> 00:42:58,233
I'll explain later!

1088
00:42:58,233 --> 00:43:02,033
(doors clanking and whirring)

1089
00:43:10,467 --> 00:43:12,200
- Just gonna have to get
used to me as a bear.

1090
00:43:12,200 --> 00:43:13,500
- Oh shut up.
- Yeah right.

1091
00:43:13,500 --> 00:43:15,200
- [Old Woman] You're all
in a sweat, dear boy.

1092
00:43:15,200 --> 00:43:16,833
- Oh its really hot.

1093
00:43:16,833 --> 00:43:19,167
- Can you see some old
tumbled down houses yet?

1094
00:43:19,167 --> 00:43:20,100
- I see them.

1095
00:43:20,100 --> 00:43:21,633
- Well they're my castles, boy.

1096
00:43:21,633 --> 00:43:22,733
(Crow growls)

1097
00:43:22,733 --> 00:43:23,967
- [Mike] Yeah, stop it.

1098
00:43:23,967 --> 00:43:25,833
- Come on, hurry hurry,
or you'll catch cold.

1099
00:43:25,833 --> 00:43:26,833
Can't you feel it?

1100
00:43:26,833 --> 00:43:28,267
That cold mountain wind.

1101
00:43:28,267 --> 00:43:29,600
Come on, faster faster.

1102
00:43:29,600 --> 00:43:31,800
- [Mike] Forget the
good deed, eat her.

1103
00:43:31,800 --> 00:43:33,867
- Here we are,
we're home at last.

1104
00:43:33,867 --> 00:43:36,333
Yes at last we're home

1105
00:43:36,333 --> 00:43:38,200
and my home is my castle.

1106
00:43:38,200 --> 00:43:41,033
I'm much obliged to
you my handsome prince.

1107
00:43:41,033 --> 00:43:42,333
- [Tom] Most bears
don't carry compacts.

1108
00:43:42,333 --> 00:43:43,567
- Look, granny.
- True.

1109
00:43:43,567 --> 00:43:44,600
- Are you making fun of me?

1110
00:43:44,600 --> 00:43:46,067
- Of course not.

1111
00:43:46,067 --> 00:43:47,433
- [Ivan] Look at me before
you call me handsome.

1112
00:43:47,433 --> 00:43:48,267
- I like that.
- I can't very well

1113
00:43:48,267 --> 00:43:49,467
do that, my boy.

1114
00:43:49,467 --> 00:43:52,067
Its been at least,
yes its been 10 years

1115
00:43:52,067 --> 00:43:53,633
since I last looked
at something.

1116
00:43:53,633 --> 00:43:55,700
You see, I'm blind.

1117
00:43:55,700 --> 00:43:58,500
- [Ivan] Oh grandma, I wish I
could of gone blind for you.

1118
00:43:58,500 --> 00:44:00,233
- [Mike] Oh man.

1119
00:44:00,233 --> 00:44:01,033
- Oh no, how you talk.

1120
00:44:01,033 --> 00:44:02,633
- Father Mushroom lied.

1121
00:44:02,633 --> 00:44:03,800
- Who did?

1122
00:44:03,800 --> 00:44:06,733
- And I'll never
look at myself again.

1123
00:44:06,733 --> 00:44:08,300
- Oh blame the mirror.

1124
00:44:09,867 --> 00:44:12,967
- [Mike] Invasion of
the matryoshka people.

1125
00:44:14,567 --> 00:44:16,100
- What do you say, son?

1126
00:44:16,100 --> 00:44:17,100
- Let me talk.

1127
00:44:17,100 --> 00:44:18,333
He likes her very much.

1128
00:44:18,333 --> 00:44:20,433
Anybody can see she's
lovely, such beauty.

1129
00:44:20,433 --> 00:44:22,100
She's in perfect health.

1130
00:44:22,100 --> 00:44:23,233
I tell you all over.

1131
00:44:24,267 --> 00:44:26,167
- [Tom] She's
imprinting on the geese.

1132
00:44:26,167 --> 00:44:27,100
- Oh hurry.

1133
00:44:28,367 --> 00:44:30,300
(laughs)

1134
00:44:30,300 --> 00:44:32,867
- And the freelance
shame squad is there.

1135
00:44:34,367 --> 00:44:35,633
- [Tom] Oh the pond scum
is fleeing in terror

1136
00:44:35,633 --> 00:44:36,867
from her face.

1137
00:44:36,867 --> 00:44:38,233
- Marfusha, my darling daughter.

1138
00:44:38,233 --> 00:44:39,067
- Help!

1139
00:44:40,200 --> 00:44:41,033
Mama!

1140
00:44:42,233 --> 00:44:44,300
- [Mike] People's
distress is funny.

1141
00:44:46,467 --> 00:44:48,067
- [Tom] She caught
a water moccasin.

1142
00:44:48,067 --> 00:44:49,633
(shouts in Russian)

1143
00:44:49,633 --> 00:44:50,900
- My daughter, my daughter.

1144
00:44:50,900 --> 00:44:52,167
- Help, help.

1145
00:44:52,167 --> 00:44:55,000
- Well I guess you got
to be Russo-Finnish.

1146
00:44:55,000 --> 00:44:57,833
- Mama!

1147
00:44:59,267 --> 00:45:02,067
- Look my dear, maybe you
should have tied it tighter.

1148
00:45:02,067 --> 00:45:04,233
- Forget my daughter then.

1149
00:45:04,233 --> 00:45:06,300
Oh my sweet little dear.

1150
00:45:06,300 --> 00:45:07,533
- Why?

1151
00:45:07,533 --> 00:45:09,700
There's not telling what
bride a boy will take

1152
00:45:09,700 --> 00:45:12,567
and my son's not stupid.

1153
00:45:12,567 --> 00:45:14,600
He's ready to take a wife.

1154
00:45:14,600 --> 00:45:15,500
Aren't you?

1155
00:45:15,500 --> 00:45:17,433
- [Tom] Duh, I guh.

1156
00:45:17,433 --> 00:45:18,800
- That one.

1157
00:45:18,800 --> 00:45:20,233
(sobs)

1158
00:45:20,233 --> 00:45:21,933
- [Mike] The private
pain of Alfred E. Neuman.

1159
00:45:21,933 --> 00:45:24,100
(sobbing)

1160
00:45:25,967 --> 00:45:27,167
- He likes her.

1161
00:45:28,600 --> 00:45:29,867
- [Tom] One of the greatest
criminal masterminds

1162
00:45:29,867 --> 00:45:31,133
of the 20th century.

1163
00:45:31,133 --> 00:45:33,967
- She makes Olivia Hussy
look like Thelma Ritter.

1164
00:45:35,233 --> 00:45:37,433
- Nastenka's the one I want.

1165
00:45:37,433 --> 00:45:38,767
(laughs goofily)

1166
00:45:38,767 --> 00:45:40,033
(mock laughter)

1167
00:45:40,033 --> 00:45:41,600
- [Mike] We're gonna
starve this winter.

1168
00:45:43,000 --> 00:45:45,300
- [Tom] Well I suppose we
should get back to being ugly.

1169
00:45:45,300 --> 00:45:48,233
- [Mike] Let's go frighten
small children, shall we?

1170
00:45:48,233 --> 00:45:49,567
(growling)

1171
00:45:49,567 --> 00:45:50,867
- Chewbacca?

1172
00:45:50,867 --> 00:45:52,400
Where are you?

1173
00:45:52,400 --> 00:45:53,533
- [Tom] Hornets
don't make honey.

1174
00:45:53,533 --> 00:45:55,467
I found out the hard way.

1175
00:45:56,933 --> 00:45:59,300
- [Crow] Mommy, can
I go play at Timmy's?

1176
00:46:01,167 --> 00:46:03,367
- [Tom] Did I have to
eat all those campers?

1177
00:46:04,367 --> 00:46:06,400
- A stick, granny's stick.

1178
00:46:06,400 --> 00:46:09,700
How is she going to be
able to walk without it?

1179
00:46:09,700 --> 00:46:11,700
- I don't know, Richard Burton.

1180
00:46:11,700 --> 00:46:13,400
- I've got to take it to her.

1181
00:46:15,533 --> 00:46:17,800
- Very good, Ivan Lushka.

1182
00:46:17,800 --> 00:46:18,633
Very good.

1183
00:46:18,633 --> 00:46:19,467
- Oh man.

1184
00:46:21,233 --> 00:46:23,633
- [Mike] Scott Hamilton's
interpretation of
the Three Bears.

1185
00:46:25,033 --> 00:46:27,667
- [Tom] Mushroom guy's
staring to piss me off.

1186
00:46:27,667 --> 00:46:28,867
- Maybe I'm dreaming.

1187
00:46:28,867 --> 00:46:31,100
Maybe its just a vision.

1188
00:46:31,100 --> 00:46:33,800
Maybe that old magician
was only bragging.

1189
00:46:33,800 --> 00:46:35,500
Still, he cast a spell on me.

1190
00:46:37,100 --> 00:46:38,967
That's that feather
that brought me here.

1191
00:46:38,967 --> 00:46:41,367
- [Mike] Maybe I'm crazier
than an outhouse rat.

1192
00:46:43,400 --> 00:46:45,767
- And this is where I
first meet Nastenka.

1193
00:46:47,433 --> 00:46:49,200
- [Crow] Help me
Obi Wan Kenoboski.

1194
00:46:52,467 --> 00:46:55,367
- [Tom] Well got a great
stick out of the deal.

1195
00:46:55,367 --> 00:46:56,700
- There's that old stump

1196
00:46:56,700 --> 00:46:59,267
and the flowers
have really bloomed

1197
00:46:59,267 --> 00:47:02,133
and that wicked old
magicians laughing at me,

1198
00:47:02,133 --> 00:47:05,100
I suppose, I can't
shake off his spell.

1199
00:47:05,100 --> 00:47:07,333
- [Mike] Oh geeze, I
stepped in my own scat.

1200
00:47:08,733 --> 00:47:10,400
- [Tom] Uh, what?

1201
00:47:10,400 --> 00:47:11,800
Very confusing lesson.

1202
00:47:11,800 --> 00:47:13,300
- [Mike] So if you
speculate about doing good

1203
00:47:13,300 --> 00:47:14,833
its better than
actually doing it?

1204
00:47:14,833 --> 00:47:16,100
- Apparently.

1205
00:47:16,100 --> 00:47:18,500
- There's only one thing
I still have to do.

1206
00:47:18,500 --> 00:47:20,200
- Join the band Nelson.

1207
00:47:21,633 --> 00:47:22,733
- Farewell, Dash...

1208
00:47:24,367 --> 00:47:25,367
(tense music)

1209
00:47:25,367 --> 00:47:27,067
- [Mike] Salmon!

1210
00:47:27,067 --> 00:47:32,067
(tense classical music)
(Tom shouting rhythmically)

1211
00:47:33,800 --> 00:47:34,833
- Well that's taken care of,

1212
00:47:34,833 --> 00:47:36,033
now what are you gonna do

1213
00:47:36,033 --> 00:47:37,233
about the fact that
you're Finnish?

1214
00:47:38,967 --> 00:47:39,900
- Nastenka!

1215
00:47:42,233 --> 00:47:43,800
- [Mike] Hello?

1216
00:47:43,800 --> 00:47:45,267
- [Narrator] The
weeks have passed,

1217
00:47:45,267 --> 00:47:47,733
the winter winds
have begun to blow.

1218
00:47:47,733 --> 00:47:50,300
The old man takes his
daughter into the heart

1219
00:47:50,300 --> 00:47:51,800
of the forest.

1220
00:47:51,800 --> 00:47:53,800
Not that he wants
to do this at all,

1221
00:47:53,800 --> 00:47:57,133
it was the cantankerous
old woman's idea.

1222
00:47:57,133 --> 00:48:01,067
She insisted for so
long, nagged for so long,

1223
00:48:01,067 --> 00:48:04,633
that the cruel old man
finally yielded to her will.

1224
00:48:04,633 --> 00:48:05,733
- [Mike] Thanks, Dad.

1225
00:48:05,733 --> 00:48:06,533
- [Stepmother
Voiceover] I keep trying

1226
00:48:06,533 --> 00:48:08,000
to get Marfusha married

1227
00:48:08,000 --> 00:48:11,000
but everybody looks at
that little viper Nastika.

1228
00:48:11,000 --> 00:48:13,467
Take her far into the
forest and lose her.

1229
00:48:13,467 --> 00:48:15,167
I never want to see her again.

1230
00:48:15,167 --> 00:48:16,433
- [Tom] Do you have to
play that tape, Dad?

1231
00:48:16,433 --> 00:48:18,233
Its a little hard
on my self esteem.

1232
00:48:20,300 --> 00:48:23,067
- Still, traffic was light
and they made good time.

1233
00:48:25,267 --> 00:48:27,567
- [Mike] Oh I hope they
invent the wheel soon.

1234
00:48:29,000 --> 00:48:31,833
- [Tom] Just hear those
sleigh bells ring a ling,

1235
00:48:31,833 --> 00:48:34,067
jing jing jingling.

1236
00:48:34,067 --> 00:48:37,233
- No, my old woman
can go right ahead

1237
00:48:37,233 --> 00:48:38,733
and kill me if she wants.

1238
00:48:38,733 --> 00:48:39,967
- Fair.

1239
00:48:39,967 --> 00:48:41,533
- But I'm not going to do this.

1240
00:48:41,533 --> 00:48:43,333
Not to you, my daughter.

1241
00:48:43,333 --> 00:48:45,633
I won't leave you in the woods.

1242
00:48:45,633 --> 00:48:47,467
Oh, Zornaka, go.

1243
00:48:47,467 --> 00:48:49,067
Come on, boy, we're going back.

1244
00:48:49,067 --> 00:48:50,567
Go!

1245
00:48:50,567 --> 00:48:52,400
- [Mike] You sure this is
convenient for you, Dad?

1246
00:48:53,800 --> 00:48:57,633
- Oh Zornaka, I don't care
if she waves the poker at me,

1247
00:48:57,633 --> 00:49:00,167
or the pitchfork.

1248
00:49:00,167 --> 00:49:03,200
Let her rave, I'm
not afraid anymore.

1249
00:49:03,200 --> 00:49:06,400
No my darling daughter,
I'm not afraid anymore!

1250
00:49:06,400 --> 00:49:09,200
I'll tell her what
I think, you'll see.

1251
00:49:09,200 --> 00:49:11,367
Ho, Zornaka. Ho.

1252
00:49:11,367 --> 00:49:13,267
- He has the spine
of a tube worm.

1253
00:49:13,267 --> 00:49:14,467
- [Nastenka
Voiceover] She's going

1254
00:49:14,467 --> 00:49:15,800
to make my poor
daddy so miserable.

1255
00:49:16,633 --> 00:49:18,300
She'll drive him mad.

1256
00:49:19,700 --> 00:49:21,700
Goodbye, daddy.

1257
00:49:21,700 --> 00:49:22,933
- [Mike] Still, it
was good for him

1258
00:49:22,933 --> 00:49:24,833
to get out of the
basement for awhile.

1259
00:49:24,833 --> 00:49:27,833
- [Nastenka Voiceover] Remember
your daughter who loved you.

1260
00:49:29,033 --> 00:49:30,967
- [Tom] Val Kilmer
as Prince Valiant.

1261
00:49:30,967 --> 00:49:31,800
- Nastia!

1262
00:49:33,100 --> 00:49:34,400
- [Mike] I need a haircut!

1263
00:49:38,900 --> 00:49:40,167
(laughs)

1264
00:49:40,167 --> 00:49:41,667
- Wolves are just
laughing out loud.

1265
00:49:41,667 --> 00:49:44,000
They got the B squad
in to eat this guy.

1266
00:49:45,233 --> 00:49:49,133
- [Tom] Fresh is
better, get Mentos fresh

1267
00:49:49,133 --> 00:49:50,400
and full of life.

1268
00:49:51,600 --> 00:49:54,267
- [Mike] What would you
do for a Klondike Bar?

1269
00:49:54,267 --> 00:49:57,833
(tense classical music)

1270
00:49:57,833 --> 00:49:59,400
- Oh, damn potholes.

1271
00:50:02,233 --> 00:50:03,067
- Nastia!

1272
00:50:05,000 --> 00:50:08,333
(mimics engine revving)

1273
00:50:09,667 --> 00:50:11,067
- You over there at the house,

1274
00:50:11,067 --> 00:50:12,500
come on, get moving.

1275
00:50:12,500 --> 00:50:14,500
Open the doors wide.

1276
00:50:14,500 --> 00:50:16,867
- [Crow] That horse
is not a real blonde.

1277
00:50:16,867 --> 00:50:18,200
- Oh, Zornaka.

1278
00:50:18,200 --> 00:50:19,400
- Mama.

1279
00:50:19,400 --> 00:50:21,067
- What's the matter with you?

1280
00:50:21,067 --> 00:50:22,400
- That's enough.

1281
00:50:22,400 --> 00:50:24,167
I'm not putting up
with this anymore.

1282
00:50:24,167 --> 00:50:25,400
Now its my...

1283
00:50:25,400 --> 00:50:27,500
- [Mike] Turn to get
down in the basement.

1284
00:50:27,500 --> 00:50:30,733
- I won't say it, I'll be quiet.

1285
00:50:30,733 --> 00:50:31,967
(laughing)

1286
00:50:31,967 --> 00:50:34,633
- Marfusha, go on
into the house.

1287
00:50:34,633 --> 00:50:36,633
You will catch a cold, darling.

1288
00:50:36,633 --> 00:50:37,667
(laughs)

1289
00:50:37,667 --> 00:50:38,900
(Crow growls)

1290
00:50:38,900 --> 00:50:40,200
you better watch out.

1291
00:50:41,833 --> 00:50:43,100
- Well I showed her.

1292
00:50:43,100 --> 00:50:44,733
Read her the riot
act, all right.

1293
00:50:44,733 --> 00:50:46,033
Yup.

1294
00:50:46,033 --> 00:50:47,300
- Nastenka's gone.

1295
00:50:47,300 --> 00:50:49,600
- [Tom] I got more you
and I've been neutered.

1296
00:50:51,300 --> 00:50:53,233
- [Mike] Don't touch
me, you coward.

1297
00:50:55,467 --> 00:50:57,167
- [Tom] Someone's
pickling something.

1298
00:50:57,167 --> 00:50:58,267
- Hey, not a bear anymore.

1299
00:50:58,267 --> 00:50:59,933
Mushroom guy turned me back.

1300
00:50:59,933 --> 00:51:00,767
- [Mike] Really?

1301
00:51:02,033 --> 00:51:03,367
You didn't just peel it off?

1302
00:51:03,367 --> 00:51:04,667
- No.

1303
00:51:04,667 --> 00:51:07,367
(tense music)

1304
00:51:07,367 --> 00:51:08,633
- [Mike] Wow.

1305
00:51:08,633 --> 00:51:11,500
- Oh little cabin, turn
your back to the forest

1306
00:51:11,500 --> 00:51:13,133
and turn your face to me.

1307
00:51:13,133 --> 00:51:14,767
- [Mike] Big Bird got developed.

1308
00:51:14,767 --> 00:51:16,600
(squawking)

1309
00:51:16,600 --> 00:51:18,000
This guys actually Jamaican.

1310
00:51:20,467 --> 00:51:22,367
- [Tom] Al Lewis, survivalist.

1311
00:51:22,367 --> 00:51:24,933
(yawns)

1312
00:51:24,933 --> 00:51:27,400
- [Baba Yaga] What do you want?

1313
00:51:27,400 --> 00:51:29,633
- She's 800 years young.

1314
00:51:29,633 --> 00:51:30,567
- Ah, Ivan.

1315
00:51:31,467 --> 00:51:33,333
Why did you come here?

1316
00:51:33,333 --> 00:51:35,033
You were not invited.

1317
00:51:35,033 --> 00:51:37,100
Now you turn my house around

1318
00:51:37,100 --> 00:51:39,833
and awaken me out
of a sound sleep.

1319
00:51:39,833 --> 00:51:41,500
The house had its back to you.

1320
00:51:41,500 --> 00:51:43,600
Whatever made you
turn it around?

1321
00:51:43,600 --> 00:51:46,100
- Oh don't be angry, hunchback
fairy, don't be angry.

1322
00:51:46,100 --> 00:51:47,133
(laughing)

1323
00:51:47,133 --> 00:51:48,733
Help me to find Nastenka.

1324
00:51:48,733 --> 00:51:49,700
I must save her.

1325
00:51:49,700 --> 00:51:51,400
Please, she needs help badly.

1326
00:51:51,400 --> 00:51:53,233
- Don't expect any
help from me, Ivan.

1327
00:51:53,233 --> 00:51:55,233
I won't give you
the slightest help.

1328
00:51:55,233 --> 00:51:57,167
- [Tom] Oh chuckles
is over here.

1329
00:51:57,167 --> 00:51:59,000
- Now my little house.

1330
00:51:59,000 --> 00:52:00,233
(bell rings)

1331
00:52:00,233 --> 00:52:01,733
About face.

1332
00:52:01,733 --> 00:52:05,100
Turn your back to Ivan
and face the woods again.

1333
00:52:05,100 --> 00:52:06,433
- [Mike] Oh its
Bill Gate's house.

1334
00:52:06,433 --> 00:52:07,667
Its voice controlled.

1335
00:52:07,667 --> 00:52:09,633
- Turn your back to
the woods and face me.

1336
00:52:09,633 --> 00:52:12,433
- Face the woods, turn
your back to Ivan.

1337
00:52:12,433 --> 00:52:14,867
- House, face me with
your back to the woods.

1338
00:52:14,867 --> 00:52:17,733
- Face the woods, turn
your back to Ivan.

1339
00:52:17,733 --> 00:52:21,000
- Come to Knott's Berryfarm
and ride the unstable house.

1340
00:52:22,267 --> 00:52:24,467
- You hooligan.

1341
00:52:24,467 --> 00:52:26,033
- I don't care how hard you try.

1342
00:52:26,033 --> 00:52:28,067
I'm going to have
the upper hand.

1343
00:52:28,067 --> 00:52:28,900
Face me!

1344
00:52:28,900 --> 00:52:30,567
- Face the woods.

1345
00:52:30,567 --> 00:52:32,167
- [Mike] Oh no.

1346
00:52:32,167 --> 00:52:33,767
No, no leg kicks please.

1347
00:52:33,767 --> 00:52:35,067
- Face me.
- Face the woods.

1348
00:52:35,067 --> 00:52:37,067
- Face me.
- Face the woods

1349
00:52:37,067 --> 00:52:38,100
- Face me.
- Face the woods.

1350
00:52:38,100 --> 00:52:39,333
- Face me.
- Face the uh...

1351
00:52:39,333 --> 00:52:41,400
- [Tom] All right,
come up for a beer.

1352
00:52:41,400 --> 00:52:42,233
- All right.

1353
00:52:43,367 --> 00:52:46,333
You'll see, won't always
have the upper hand.

1354
00:52:46,333 --> 00:52:50,000
Your strength is only
earthly strength.

1355
00:52:50,000 --> 00:52:51,900
In the end it won't help.

1356
00:52:51,900 --> 00:52:54,467
Like ours use witch kind.

1357
00:52:54,467 --> 00:52:55,467
(creaking)

1358
00:52:55,467 --> 00:52:57,167
- Please.
- Don't.

1359
00:52:57,167 --> 00:52:59,033
- [Mike] Don't do that.

1360
00:52:59,033 --> 00:53:01,433
- Don't give up yet,
my young knight.

1361
00:53:01,433 --> 00:53:03,333
- [Mike] His performance
is so wooden.

1362
00:53:05,233 --> 00:53:08,200
- Quick, give him
Dutch Elm disease.

1363
00:53:08,200 --> 00:53:11,200
- [Tom] This is an
Earth First fantasy.

1364
00:53:11,200 --> 00:53:13,100
- [Mike] Take that,
logging industry.

1365
00:53:15,500 --> 00:53:18,167
- I've heard that tree gang
violence is increasing.

1366
00:53:19,867 --> 00:53:21,200
(laughs)

1367
00:53:21,200 --> 00:53:22,467
- [Mike] Don't you.

1368
00:53:22,467 --> 00:53:23,733
- [Tom] Oh they got
him in a hodi ring.

1369
00:53:25,833 --> 00:53:27,667
- [Mike] Miracle-Gro
worked too well.

1370
00:53:29,133 --> 00:53:30,733
- [Trees] One, two.

1371
00:53:33,167 --> 00:53:34,833
Three!

1372
00:53:34,833 --> 00:53:36,333
- [Tom] In you pixies
go, through the door,

1373
00:53:36,333 --> 00:53:37,600
through the window.

1374
00:53:38,667 --> 00:53:40,667
- Oh self delivering lumber.

1375
00:53:42,800 --> 00:53:44,667
- [Mike] I just hate it
when the trees just come in.

1376
00:53:44,667 --> 00:53:47,300
- [Tom] If I had a tree,
I'd keep it in the yard.

1377
00:53:47,300 --> 00:53:49,467
- This way, right this way.

1378
00:53:49,467 --> 00:53:52,800
You make a find roast, all nice.

1379
00:53:52,800 --> 00:53:54,600
- [Crow] Uh oh,
roasted nuts, oh boy.

1380
00:53:54,600 --> 00:53:56,400
- Ivan, you can't win.

1381
00:53:56,400 --> 00:53:59,167
Struggle Ivan, come on
fight back all you like.

1382
00:53:59,167 --> 00:54:00,533
Nothings going to stop me.

1383
00:54:00,533 --> 00:54:02,200
You're my supper.

1384
00:54:02,200 --> 00:54:04,133
- Look, hunchback
fairy, I'm sorry.

1385
00:54:04,133 --> 00:54:05,333
- Are you afraid?

1386
00:54:05,333 --> 00:54:06,667
- Well I've never
been pushed in an oven

1387
00:54:06,667 --> 00:54:08,900
and its the first
I've sat on a shovel.

1388
00:54:08,900 --> 00:54:10,333
- [Mike] The flat part anyway.

1389
00:54:10,333 --> 00:54:12,000
(cackles)

1390
00:54:12,000 --> 00:54:13,867
- Please show me how
to sit on a shovel.

1391
00:54:13,867 --> 00:54:15,333
I don't know.

1392
00:54:15,333 --> 00:54:16,833
- [Tom] Hello, Mrs. Non Gorilla.

1393
00:54:16,833 --> 00:54:18,733
- Take the handle.

1394
00:54:18,733 --> 00:54:19,667
- All right.

1395
00:54:19,667 --> 00:54:21,167
- What's the world coming to?

1396
00:54:21,167 --> 00:54:23,367
The youth of today
wasn't taught anything.

1397
00:54:23,367 --> 00:54:27,167
You see, you don't have to be
a wizard to do that, stupid.

1398
00:54:27,167 --> 00:54:28,767
- I hope its warm
enough for you.

1399
00:54:28,767 --> 00:54:29,900
(shouts)

1400
00:54:29,900 --> 00:54:31,400
- [Baba Yaga] I'm cooking!

1401
00:54:31,400 --> 00:54:32,667
I'm roasting.

1402
00:54:32,667 --> 00:54:34,600
(shouting)

1403
00:54:34,600 --> 00:54:35,533
- All right, get out of here.

1404
00:54:35,533 --> 00:54:38,133
I'll turn you all into kindling.

1405
00:54:38,133 --> 00:54:40,200
Go on, get out.

1406
00:54:40,200 --> 00:54:42,867
Now run for your lives.

1407
00:54:42,867 --> 00:54:46,667
(Mike humming Benny Hill theme)

1408
00:54:46,667 --> 00:54:48,467
- [Tom] Split up,
its our only hope.

1409
00:54:50,133 --> 00:54:52,000
- [Crow] Oh I forgot
to preheat the oven.

1410
00:54:52,000 --> 00:54:53,667
- Its hot in here!

1411
00:54:53,667 --> 00:54:55,533
I'm sizzling.

1412
00:54:55,533 --> 00:54:56,800
- [Mike] Is this weird
or is it just me?

1413
00:54:56,800 --> 00:54:58,700
- A steam bath
never hurt anybody.

1414
00:54:58,700 --> 00:55:00,900
And now tell me, where is she?

1415
00:55:00,900 --> 00:55:02,800
Tell me where I
can find Nastenka.

1416
00:55:02,800 --> 00:55:04,033
- Geeze.

1417
00:55:04,033 --> 00:55:06,533
- Tell me how I
can save Nastenka.

1418
00:55:06,533 --> 00:55:07,733
- Oh save her, save her.

1419
00:55:07,733 --> 00:55:09,167
- All right, you old
witch, in you go again.

1420
00:55:09,167 --> 00:55:10,500
- No.

1421
00:55:10,500 --> 00:55:11,433
- [Mike] Robert
Mapplethorpe's Strega Nona.

1422
00:55:11,433 --> 00:55:12,633
- You cook a little longer.

1423
00:55:12,633 --> 00:55:13,667
- No, Ivan, no.

1424
00:55:13,667 --> 00:55:15,500
- [Tom] What.

1425
00:55:15,500 --> 00:55:16,933
I mean when, whom.

1426
00:55:16,933 --> 00:55:18,100
I'm sorry, who.

1427
00:55:20,033 --> 00:55:24,500
- Later, in twinkly
winkly pixie wixie land.

1428
00:55:24,500 --> 00:55:29,500
(singing in Russian)
(whimsical music)

1429
00:55:33,733 --> 00:55:36,100
- [Mike] Hey Jack
Frost, finally.

1430
00:55:36,100 --> 00:55:38,067
- Wanna translate, Tom?

1431
00:55:38,067 --> 00:55:40,400
- [Tom] Its colder than
a bucket of penguin poop.

1432
00:55:40,400 --> 00:55:42,200
Its colder than a
polar bear's butt.

1433
00:55:42,200 --> 00:55:45,267
The dogs are sticking
to the fire hydrants.

1434
00:55:46,600 --> 00:55:47,600
- Bye bye.

1435
00:55:47,600 --> 00:55:49,200
- [Tom] That means bye bye.

1436
00:55:49,200 --> 00:55:50,033
- Thank you.

1437
00:55:51,500 --> 00:55:53,067
- [Mike] What do
you want, Frost?

1438
00:55:53,067 --> 00:55:56,000
(speaking Russian)

1439
00:55:59,800 --> 00:56:02,633
- Hey, he can make
the film reverse.

1440
00:56:02,633 --> 00:56:04,833
(speaking Russian)

1441
00:56:04,833 --> 00:56:06,133
- [Mike] We will bury you.

1442
00:56:08,600 --> 00:56:10,733
- I do frost and I do it well.

1443
00:56:10,733 --> 00:56:12,567
- [Tom] At least its not
a film about Jack Abcess.

1444
00:56:14,233 --> 00:56:16,033
- [Mike] Eat lead, Spring.

1445
00:56:17,500 --> 00:56:20,500
- [Tom] Frosty lucky trees,
they're magically delicious.

1446
00:56:20,500 --> 00:56:23,367
- So he bought a flocking gun?

1447
00:56:23,367 --> 00:56:24,200
Big deal.

1448
00:56:25,600 --> 00:56:29,500
- [Mike] Jack Frost opened fire
on a stand of willows today.

1449
00:56:29,500 --> 00:56:30,667
- [Tom] I don't really need, um,

1450
00:56:30,667 --> 00:56:31,967
its gonna ruin my buds.

1451
00:56:31,967 --> 00:56:32,800
Oh I'm dead.

1452
00:56:35,400 --> 00:56:36,800
- [Mike] You know,
I'm from Wisconsin.

1453
00:56:36,800 --> 00:56:37,633
I've seen plenty of this.

1454
00:56:37,633 --> 00:56:38,700
Can we move on?

1455
00:56:40,200 --> 00:56:42,333
- Smilla's sense of crap.

1456
00:56:42,333 --> 00:56:44,867
- [Tom] Although the director
left this somewhat ambiguous

1457
00:56:44,867 --> 00:56:47,467
I'm getting the idea
that he's frosting trees.

1458
00:56:47,467 --> 00:56:48,300
- Could be.

1459
00:56:50,167 --> 00:56:52,200
Don't frost her, you big.

1460
00:56:52,200 --> 00:56:54,400
- [Mike] I pray for the
death of Jack Frost.

1461
00:56:56,567 --> 00:56:59,400
- [Tom] You work for
summer, don't ya, don't ya!

1462
00:57:03,533 --> 00:57:06,733
- Where did this little
marvel come from?

1463
00:57:06,733 --> 00:57:09,433
Little girl, where
were you until now?

1464
00:57:09,433 --> 00:57:10,833
- Back off, Frost.

1465
00:57:10,833 --> 00:57:12,700
- I, at home.

1466
00:57:12,700 --> 00:57:13,533
- At home.

1467
00:57:14,667 --> 00:57:17,833
Tell me, don't you feel cold?

1468
00:57:17,833 --> 00:57:20,433
- Oh I feel warm enough,
grandfather Frost.

1469
00:57:20,433 --> 00:57:21,967
- [Frost] You're warm?

1470
00:57:21,967 --> 00:57:23,167
- I'm warm.

1471
00:57:23,167 --> 00:57:26,233
- [Mike] Look, I've got mace.

1472
00:57:26,233 --> 00:57:28,267
- [Tom] My muffins!

1473
00:57:28,267 --> 00:57:30,500
(coughing)

1474
00:57:32,033 --> 00:57:33,633
- Oh god, my heart.

1475
00:57:34,533 --> 00:57:36,767
- Even now are you warm?

1476
00:57:36,767 --> 00:57:37,700
Graceful creature.

1477
00:57:38,667 --> 00:57:41,633
- I'm warm, Grandfather Frost.

1478
00:57:41,633 --> 00:57:43,300
I am warm, grandfather.

1479
00:57:43,300 --> 00:57:46,233
- [Mike] Am I gonna
have to call the cops?

1480
00:57:46,233 --> 00:57:48,300
- You're a very good girl.

1481
00:57:48,300 --> 00:57:50,500
Not the contradicting kind.

1482
00:57:50,500 --> 00:57:51,367
- [Tom] Yes I am.

1483
00:57:52,800 --> 00:57:56,500
- Here you are, my little
marvel, here's my cloak.

1484
00:57:56,500 --> 00:57:58,300
- It smells like dried Ensure.

1485
00:57:59,167 --> 00:58:01,133
- How bout you then?

1486
00:58:01,133 --> 00:58:02,500
You'll be cold.

1487
00:58:02,500 --> 00:58:03,567
- Me, cold?

1488
00:58:03,567 --> 00:58:05,200
(laughing)
- Why, I'm made

1489
00:58:05,200 --> 00:58:06,433
of fleshy Thinsulate.

1490
00:58:06,433 --> 00:58:08,667
(laughing)

1491
00:58:11,400 --> 00:58:12,233
- A bird.

1492
00:58:12,233 --> 00:58:13,067
- Lets eat it.

1493
00:58:16,800 --> 00:58:20,633
- [Mike] Wow, bottom line,
don't mess with Jack Frost.

1494
00:58:20,633 --> 00:58:23,900
- Don't bother, my sweet,
it won't do any good.

1495
00:58:23,900 --> 00:58:25,433
- [Mike] Its dead, dead.

1496
00:58:25,433 --> 00:58:28,533
- In my magic scepter lies the
power that spreads the frost.

1497
00:58:28,533 --> 00:58:30,567
- You have no pity.

1498
00:58:30,567 --> 00:58:31,933
You're cruel.

1499
00:58:31,933 --> 00:58:33,933
- Oh I am not at
all without pity.

1500
00:58:33,933 --> 00:58:35,200
I am not cruel.

1501
00:58:35,200 --> 00:58:37,067
I do pity this poor
little frozen bird.

1502
00:58:37,067 --> 00:58:41,767
But any living creature who
touches my magic scepter

1503
00:58:41,767 --> 00:58:44,433
will never wake up again.

1504
00:58:44,433 --> 00:58:46,267
- Admittedly its
a design flaw but.

1505
00:58:46,267 --> 00:58:48,433
- What's the matter, my sweet?

1506
00:58:48,433 --> 00:58:50,333
- Goodbye, Grandfather Frost.

1507
00:58:50,333 --> 00:58:52,567
- [Frost] What's
wrong, pretty one?

1508
00:58:52,567 --> 00:58:53,567
- I'm freezing.

1509
00:58:53,567 --> 00:58:55,100
- Who, who who!

1510
00:58:55,100 --> 00:58:56,167
I say.

1511
00:58:56,167 --> 00:58:58,367
Quickly, quickly, my ice sleigh.

1512
00:58:59,467 --> 00:59:00,567
- [Tom] Whoa.

1513
00:59:00,567 --> 00:59:01,833
- Like the wind.

1514
00:59:01,833 --> 00:59:03,867
- [Tom] I think you
got an engine fire.

1515
00:59:03,867 --> 00:59:05,267
(Jack Frost mimic
engine revving)

1516
00:59:05,267 --> 00:59:06,633
- He's making that sound.

1517
00:59:06,633 --> 00:59:09,867
- [Mike] The new
1976 Chevy Sleigh.

1518
00:59:09,867 --> 00:59:13,500
